OVERVIEW

--------

This update prepares EMA_Crossover_EA.mq5 for automated paper trading on

MetaTrader 5. Building on the prior crossover array-indexing fix, v1.02

resolves edge-case bugs around stale trade signals, dropped bars on

reconnect, broker stop-level validation, and order status logging.





SUMMARY OF CHANGES (v1.02)

--------------------------



1. Prevented Stale / Delayed Crossover Entries

   - Previously, once a bullish EMA crossover was detected, the armed flag

     (g_bullishCrossDetected) stayed true indefinitely if the trade was

     blocked by trading hours, weekday filters, or an open position. This

     could cause a late BUY entry hours or days after the crossover.

   - Updated UpdateCrossoverState() to reset g_bullishCrossDetected to

     false on any bar where a new bullish crossover did not occur.



2. Prevented Silent Bar Skips on Startup or Reconnect

   - Previously, if CopyBuffer() failed while MT5 was loading chart history

     or reconnecting, OnTick() still updated g_lastBarTime and skipped the

     completed bar permanently.

   - Changed UpdateCrossoverState() to return a bool indicating whether

     indicator data loaded successfully.

   - Added a guard in OnTick() to ignore empty bar timestamps

     (currentBarTime == 0) and exit early on buffer read failure so the

     EA retries on the next tick.



3. Improved Broker Stop-Loss / Take-Profit Validation

   - Previously, SL and TP distances were validated before tick-size

     rounding and without accounting for the spread between Ask and Bid.

     Because MT5 validates BUY stop levels against Bid, tight stops during

     wide spreads could fail with retcode 10016 (Invalid Stops).

   - Moved SL/TP calculation and tick-size normalization ahead of

     validation, then verified that final SL is below Bid, final TP is

     above Bid, and both distances from Bid satisfy the broker's minimum

     stops level.



4. Added Automated Trading Permission Checks

   - Added a startup warning in OnInit() if Algo Trading is turned off in

     MT5 or the EA properties.

   - Added a pre-trade check in TryOpenBuy() using TERMINAL_TRADE_ALLOWED

     and MQL_TRADE_ALLOWED to log a clear error instead of sending a

     rejected order.



5. Added Explicit Order Execution Retcode Verification

   - Updated TryOpenBuy() to verify trade.ResultRetcode() against

     TRADE_RETCODE_DONE, TRADE_RETCODE_DONE_PARTIAL, and

     TRADE_RETCODE_PLACED rather than relying solely on the boolean return

     of trade.Buy().



6. Expanded Diagnostic Logging & Corrected Comments

   - Added clear Experts-tab log messages in OnTick() whenever a detected

     bullish crossover is skipped (outside trading hours, disabled weekday,

     or max open positions already reached).

   - Standardized decimal formatting in log outputs using DoubleToString()

     for prices, lots, and margin figures.

   - Updated #property version to "1.02".

   - Corrected inline comments in UpdateCrossoverState() to accurately

     describe MQL5 non-series static array order (index 0 = older bar at

     shift 2; index 1 = most recent completed bar at shift 1) and fixed

     the header comment on HasNoOpenPosition().





NOTES FOR REPOSITORY USERS

--------------------------

- Recompile EMA_Crossover_EA.mq5 in MetaEditor (F7) after pulling this

  update so MetaTrader 5 uses the new .ex5 binary.

- This update does not change the core strategy (Fast EMA 40 / Slow EMA

  200 bullish crossover, BUY-only, static SL/TP) or existing input

  parameters.

- Reminder: Use paper trading (demo accounts) only.
